tag example;

saved: ?*int = null;

stash() noregion {
    saved = new int[1](1)
}

main(): int {
    callback: fn() noregion = &stash;
    callback();
    0
}

/* expect compile {|
noregion_indirect_call.l8:11:5

    callback();
    ^^^^^^^^

main calls a function value, which requires noregion and cannot run
inside a region.

If this restriction is intended, declare main as noregion. Its callers
also need noregion. This prevents those functions from being called
inside a region.

If this function should remain usable inside a region, call a function
that does not require noregion instead. For a callee you own, keeping
its temporary allocations local may remove that restriction.

|} */
